# Native image builds

This Mac is ARM. The live host is amd64 Alma Linux (`jsevans@news.theuse.net`, repo at `/data/containers/OpenUsenetServer`). QEMU/`docker build --platform linux/amd64` on the Mac has crashed the Go compiler.

When building or uploading `jsevans/openusenet`:

1. Rsync the working tree to the news box (exclude `.env` and `docker-compose.override.yml`).
2. `podman build` natively on that host.
3. Push/tag from there (`jsevans/openusenet:<version>` and `:latest`), or load the image for Hub push if the host is not logged in.
4. Recreate the `openusenet` container on the news box after a successful build.

Do not start Colima or use buildx emulation for this image.
